### Objection 1 (Critical): CSS Specificity Cascade Failure

- **What is wrong**: The plan requires every scene CSS rule to be scoped to `.scene[data-scene="N"]` in `scenes/<slug>.css`, while keeping the existing `renderer.css` as the shared base. However, almost every rule in the live Color Polish pass in `renderer.css` is prefixed with `#tv`.
- **Why it matters**: In CSS cascade specificity, an ID selector (`#tv .day`, `#tv .edu-card`, `#tv .stat-expression`, `#tv .orbit-sun`, etc.) has specificity `(0, 1, 1, 0)`. A class-scoped rule like `.scene[data-scene="5"] .day` has specificity `(0, 0, 2, 0)`. The ID selector in `renderer.css` strictly overrides the class rule regardless of load order. Because scene lanes are strictly forbidden from editing `renderer.css`, any visual refinements written by scene writers into `scenes/<slug>.css` will be silently discarded and ignored by the browser.
- **Evidence**:
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md line 32](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L32): "every scene CSS rule scoped to .scene[data-scene="N"] (arrival: .event-stage)."
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md line 74](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L74): "the existing renderer.css stays as the shared base."
  - [public/color-polish/renderer.css lines 152 to 251](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/public/color-polish/renderer.css#L152): `#tv .edu-card`, `#tv .day`, `#tv .stat-expression`, `#tv .orbit-sun`, `#tv .progress-milestone .threshold`, and dozens of others all use `#tv`.

