### Objection 2 (Critical): Scene Numbering Inversion Trap (Section Number vs Renderer ID)

- **What is wrong**: The plan labels sections according to Anthony's campaign list (Section 6: We Are Peacemakers, Section 7: Status, Section 8: Nine Expressions). However, the internal renderer IDs are completely different (Peacemakers is ID 8, Status is ID 6, Expressions is ID 7).
- **Why it matters**: The plan tells writers to scope rules to `.scene[data-scene="N"]`. A Gemini 3.8 Flash writer assigned to Section 6 (Peacemakers) will naturally write `.scene[data-scene="6"]`, which in the DOM is actually Participation Status! Section 7 (Status) will write `.scene[data-scene="7"]` (which targets Expressions), and Section 8 (Expressions) will write `.scene[data-scene="8"]` (which targets Peacemakers). This numbering inversion will cross-contaminate and corrupt styles across all three scenes.
- **Evidence**:
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md line 32](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L32): "every scene CSS rule scoped to .scene[data-scene="N"]"
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md line 34](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L34): "Scene id map (Anthony's number, renderer id, slug): ... 6/8 peacemakers, 7/6 status, 8/7 expressions."
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md lines 148, 160, 172](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L148): "Section 6: We Are Peacemakers", "Section 7: Status", "Section 8: Nine Expressions".
  - [public/color-polish/renderer.js line 247](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/public/color-polish/renderer.js#L247): `el.dataset.scene=id;` where `id` is the renderer ID (8 for peacemakers, 6 for status, 7 for expressions).

