### Objection 4 (High): Section 0 Scope Explosion and False Pick Independence

- **What is wrong**: Section 0 claims to be a simple "foundation split, no visual change." But to eliminate branching on scene numbers in core files, Section 0 must invent a dynamic registry interface (`registerScene`), extract all 11 scenes into standalone descriptors in `scenes/<slug>.js`, and replace all existing scene calls in one step.
- **Why it matters**: If Section 0 creates full descriptors for all 11 scenes on `tv/base`, then all 11 scenes are already refactored on `tv/base`. When Anthony uses `tv/pick` to select a subset (e.g. only Welcome and Calendar), the unselected scenes in `tv/pick` do not run the battle-tested monolithic `renderer.js` code; they run the brand-new, unverified Section 0 split implementations. The plan's promise that unchosen scenes remain untouched is false.
- **Evidence**:
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md line 40](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L40): "tv/pick: recreated from tv/base each time Anthony chooses a subset; merge each chosen branch. Disjoint files, no conflicts. An unchosen branch stays parked and blocks nothing."
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md lines 66 to 77](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L66): Core code must read `registerScene` descriptors instead of branching on scene numbers, requiring full extraction of all 11 scenes before any scene lane launches.

