### Objection 5 (High): Shared Scene Logic Left Unowned Across Disjoint Lanes

- **What is wrong**: The Section 0 file division (lines 66-75) omits shared helper functions that span multiple scenes. Most notably, `rightBubbles()` is shared across Welcome (Scene 1), Peacemakers (Scene 8), and Peace in Practice (Scene 9).
- **Why it matters**: If `rightBubbles()` is placed inside `scenes/welcome.js`, and Anthony creates a `tv/pick` containing Peacemakers but not Welcome, Peacemakers will crash with a runtime `ReferenceError: rightBubbles is not defined`. If multiple scene lanes define it, classic script global scope will throw a duplicate identifier error.
- **Evidence**:
  - [public/color-polish/renderer.js lines 159 to 164](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/public/color-polish/renderer.js#L159): `function rightBubbles() { ... }`
  - [public/color-polish/renderer.js lines 166, 181, 182](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/public/color-polish/renderer.js#L166): Used in `welcome()`, `peaceScene()`, and `peacemakers()`.
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md lines 67 to 75](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L67): `rightBubbles()` is omitted from the file mapping of `core/orbs.js` and all core modules.

