### Objection 6 (High): Calendar Click Delegation Conflicts with Live TV Scene Advance

- **What is wrong**: Section 0 replaces the dead inline `onclick` on calendar day buttons with a delegated event listener. However, on the live TV display, a global click listener (`document.addEventListener('click', manualAdvance)`) advances the scene on any click or tap.
- **Why it matters**: When a user clicks a calendar day on live TV, the event will trigger day selection AND bubble to `document`, immediately advancing to the next scene. If the day listener calls `event.stopPropagation()` to stop the advance, it breaks the core requirement deployed in Plan 11 that clicking anywhere on live TV advances the scene. The plan fails to define how day selection and scene advance coexist.
- **Evidence**:
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md line 79](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L79): "replace the dead inline onclick on calendar days ... with a data-day attribute and a delegated listener".
  - [public/color-polish/renderer.js lines 292 to 307 and 589](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/public/color-polish/renderer.js#L292): `manualAdvance()` executes on `document` click whenever `S.source === 'live'`.

---

### Objection 7 (Medium): Missing Rollback Strategy and Promotion Gaps

- **What is wrong**: Section 12 specifies merging `tv/pick` directly into `codex/color-polish-v6` and `codex/mothers-love` (production) after preview verification. It provides zero instructions, scripts, or commit targets for rolling back production if physical TV hardware shows rendering anomalies.
- **Why it matters**: Display rendering on real 4K smart TV web engines frequently surfaces GPU memory limits or layout bugs not visible in local headless Chromium. Without an explicit rollback mechanism, recovering from a flawed deployment requires ad hoc manual intervention.
- **Evidence**:
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md line 228](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L228): Section 12 details promotion, but contains zero rollback procedures.

---

### Objection 8 (Medium): Test Isolation and Missing Shared Admin Fixtures

- **What is wrong**: The common scene spec (line 234) requires every scene spec (`tests/color-polish-scenes/<slug>.spec.ts`) to verify that `/admin/display` renders the scene from sample data and does not advance on click. Testing `/admin/display` requires authenticated Supabase session mocking (`mockCommon`, `signInAs`, overview fixtures).
- **Why it matters**: That mocking infrastructure currently exists as private, unexported functions in `tests/color-polish-usable/usable.spec.ts`. Because Section 0 protects `tests/**`, no shared test fixture file exists. All 11 scene lanes will either duplicate 150 lines of Playwright setup or create conflicting fixtures, causing maintenance and merge friction.
- **Evidence**:
  - [PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md lines 64 and 234](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/docs/PLAN-13-tv-scene-refactor.md#L64): Section 0 protects `tests/**`, while common spec mandates testing `/admin/display`.
  - [tests/color-polish-usable/usable.spec.ts lines 63 to 104](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-critic/tests/color-polish-usable/usable.spec.ts#L63): Auth and overview mocks are unexported module internals.

